From 5b6c9d920af0dd103836c8e3603a38035c6a684d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:22:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] microblaze: remove cbranchsi4_reg

cbranchsi4_reg is not a standard pattern name, and nothing generates it,
so it and microblaze_expand_conditional_branch_reg have never run since
they were added in 2015.  They are also wrong: for EQ the expander sets
a register with pcmpeq, which gives 1 when the operands are equal, then
branches when that register is 0, so the branch is taken when they
differ.  Remove both.

The new test checks equality branches and values between registers with
-mxl-pattern-compare, the option that makes pcmpeq available, and that
pcmpeq and pcmpne are still used.  It passes with and without this
patch, because the removed code was unreachable.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/microblaze.md (cbranchsi4_reg): Remove.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
	(microblaze_expand_conditional_branch_reg): Remove.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze-protos.h
	(microblaze_expand_conditional_branch_reg): Remove.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/cbranch-eq-reg.c: New test.
